Adaptive reuse strategies enable products designed for one purpose to be repurposed for different contexts or functions, extending lifecycle beyond original intention. This approach maximizes product value by enabling secondary market applications, home modifications, or creative reinterpretation by end-users. Design for adaptive reuse requires functional flexibility, modular architecture, and aesthetic coherence that permits recombination and redeployment. Adaptive reuse exemplifies circular principles by maximizing resource utilization and keeping materials in use indefinitely.